.TH WHTML 1 "September 2026" "wellutils 1.4.0-55" "wellutils"
.SH NAME
whtml \- rich, self-contained HTML system report (offline)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B whtml
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B whtml
collects data from the wellutils suite (via their
.BR --json
output) and renders a single self-contained HTML file: Overview, CPU, GPU,
Memory, Disks & S.M.A.R.T., Peripherals, Network, Thermal, and Health.
.PP
The generated file is fully offline: it embeds all CSS/JS inline, loads no
external resources, and makes no network requests. You can open it locally or
share it as-is.
.PP
No internet access is used. (The only wellutils command that connects to the
network is
.BR wellup (1)
for self-updates \(em unrelated to this tool.)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-output " FILE"
Save the HTML report to FILE (default:
.IR ~/wellreport.html ).
.TP
.B \-\-no-open
Do not auto-open the report in a browser.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Force opening the report in a browser after generation.
.TP
.B \-\-ami
Render the report in a classic AMI BIOS setup-utility style (English only,
font and colors taken from the xb-16 BIOS emulator), instead of the default
flat CLI style.
.TP
.BR \-\-ai
Optional AI analysis, see
.B AI ENRICHMENT
below.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-lang " ru|en|auto"
Report language (auto = from the locale).
.B \-\-ami
is always English.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Shell tracing plus progress messages on stderr.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH AI ENRICHMENT
AI analysis is OPTIONAL and OFF BY DEFAULT. It activates only when you
.B explicitly
request it and supply your own endpoint:
.IP
.nf
WHTML_AI_ENDPOINT=https://your.llm.host/v1/chat/completions whtml --ai
.fi
.PP
This tool never ships a default endpoint (bring your own), so by default it
makes zero network requests. When enabled, the context sent to the endpoint is
sanitized: MAC addresses, hostnames, IPs, serial numbers and UUIDs are
stripped before anything leaves the machine. Any AI failure is ignored and the
HTML report is still produced.
.PP
The rest of the report is fully offline and read-only.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WHTML_AI_ENDPOINT
Optional. If set (and
.B --ai
is passed) the tool posts a sanitized summary to this OpenAI-compatible
endpoint. No default value.
.TP
.B WHTML_AI_MODEL
Optional model name for the endpoint (default:
.BR local-model ).
.TP
.B WELLUTILS_LANG
Force
.BR ru | en ;
otherwise the locale is used.
.TP
.B WHTML_DEBUG
Set to
.B 1
to print collection progress to stderr.
.TP
.B WHTML_KEEP_TMP
Set to
.B 1
to keep the temporary work directory (its path is printed on stderr).
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Where the work directory is created (fallbacks: /tmp, $PREFIX/tmp on Termux,
/var/tmp, $HOME).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Report written.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage (unknown option or any positional argument).
.TP
.B 3
Runtime error: python3 missing, no writable temporary directory, report
generation failed, or the output file could not be written.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.B python3
is required by this tool (and only by this tool and the PNG logo of
.BR wellfetch (1)).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wellutils (1),
.BR wellhw (1),
.BR welldoctor (1),
.BR wellup (1)
